# SQL's `using`: DS0122 with a fix to `on`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' using customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..58
  PIPELINE@0..57
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    JOIN_OP@20..57
      IDENT@20..24 "join"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      LITERAL@25..40
        STRING@25..40 "'customers.csv'"
      WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
      IDENT@41..46 "using"
      WHITESPACE@46..47 " "
      NAME_REF@47..57
        IDENT@47..57 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@57..58 "\n"

error[DS0122]: `join` uses `on`, not `using`
  --> query:1:42
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' using customerId
  |                                          ^^^^^ expected `on` here
  |
  = help: write `on` before the columns to match

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | join 'customers.csv' on customerId
which parses without errors
